---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Collapse Timeline"
  description="DeadMTL Collapse Timeline - public archive file for how Montreal fractured before Season 0."
>

<div class="page-bbs-bar" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="pbb__seg pbb__seg--active">Archive File</span>
  <span class="pbb__seg">Collapse Timeline</span>
  <span class="pbb__seg pbb__seg--sys">Access: Public</span>
  <span class="pbb__spacer"></span>
  <span class="pbb__ref">MTL COLLAPSE // 1993-1994</span>
</div>

<section class="term-hero" style="padding-block: clamp(2.5rem,6vw,5rem);">
  <div class="th__inner">
    <div class="th__eyebrow">PUBLIC ARCHIVE // COLLAPSE TIMELINE // SEASON 0</div>
    <div class="th__headline" style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem,5vw,3.5rem);">Collapse Timeline</div>
    <p class="th__body">
      A public archive outline of how Montr&eacute;al fractured before the DeadMTL Season 0 frame.
      This is an in-world archive file, not a server launch announcement.
    </p>
    <div class="th__cta">
      <a href="/knowledge/" class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">&larr; Knowledge Center</a>
      <a href="/dispatch/" class="term-btn term-btn--teal">Dispatch Archive &rsaquo;</a>
      <a href="/map/" class="term-btn term-btn--ghost">Tactical Map &rsaquo;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="municipal-notice">
      <span class="mn__stamp">Archive Boundary</span>
      <p class="mn__body">
        This timeline records reported collapse history for the DeadMTL world.
        The game server is pending. Open access is planned, not live.
        This page does not prove a playable custom Montr&eacute;al map.
      </p>
      <div class="mn__ref">Ref: DEADMTL-TIME-001 &bull; Public Archive &bull; Confidence varies by entry</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">Classification</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">How to Read the Timeline</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="taxonomy-grid">
      <div class="tax-cell">
        <div class="tc__type tc__type--field">confirmed</div>
        <div class="tc__label">Confirmed</div>
        <p class="tc__desc">Stable archive anchor. Safe to reuse in public lore and planning.</p>
        <div class="tc__world">Archive confidence</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tax-cell">
        <div class="tc__type tc__type--research">reported</div>
        <div class="tc__label">Reported</div>
        <p class="tc__desc">Useful field or civic report, but not complete certainty.</p>
        <div class="tc__world">Partial record</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tax-cell">
        <div class="tc__type tc__type--dispatch">rumored</div>
        <div class="tc__label">Rumored</div>
        <p class="tc__desc">Survivor rumor, unreliable signal, or incomplete local knowledge.</p>
        <div class="tc__world">Unstable signal</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tax-cell">
        <div class="tc__type tc__type--notice">classified</div>
        <div class="tc__label">Classified</div>
        <p class="tc__desc">Public detail withheld. The gap is part of the record.</p>
        <div class="tc__world">Redacted</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section crt-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hs__head">
      <span class="hs__label">Archive Timeline</span>
      <h2 class="hs__title">1993-1994 Collapse Sequence</h2>
      <p class="hs__sub">Grounded first. Mythic second. The exact origin remains uncertain.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Early 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">confirmed</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Montr&eacute;al is still recognizable: work, school, transit, politics, bars, factories,
          borough life, and ordinary city noise. The Canadiens win the Stanley Cup in June.
          That memory becomes one of the last shared civic reference points before the city fractures.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Summer 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported / rumored</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Outside reports become inconsistent: illness, riots, quarantine, violent incidents,
          hoaxes, American panic, and official denials. Inside Montr&eacute;al, the first strange
          reports are easy to dismiss as stress, drugs, bad information, or distant trouble.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">September 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Emergency rooms, supply chains, police response, and transit reliability begin degrading.
          Industrial corridors and canal-side service routes show missing crews, sealed loading areas,
          and unusual night movement. No single public explanation holds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">October 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Movement control becomes visible. Bridges, tunnels, hospitals, rail yards, and industrial
          roads become checkpoints or delay zones. Ville-Marie begins to harden. Local watches and
          improvised ration points appear in several neighborhoods.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Early November 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          The Pont Mercier corridor fails as a reliable control line. LaSalle becomes associated
          with sustained pressure from the south and southwest. Movement trends northeast through
          Angrignon and toward the western edge of Saint-Paul-&Eacute;mard.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">November 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Verdun closes into pockets. Rationing, route control, smuggling, and distrust define
          movement along the riverfront. Canal routes become strategically important: service lanes,
          fog, industrial crossings, and old marks matter more than official roads.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Early December 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">confirmed</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Citywide coordination fails. Boroughs, sectors, institutions, and survivor pockets begin
          acting independently. Downtown is effectively sealed. Tunnel and metro stories become
          unreliable. Montr&eacute;al is no longer behaving like one city.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel term-panel--teal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">December 1993</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">confirmed</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Saint-Paul-&Eacute;mard becomes Sector 01 because it is bounded, ugly, practical, readable,
          and not fully lost. It is not safe, but it can still be mapped. DeadMTL begins here:
          Montr&eacute;al is not recovering. It is separating into sectors, routes, sealed places,
          and pressure fronts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">1994-01-10</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Frequency 88.7 resumes with a short looping signal captured near the south end of Monk.
          The origin is not confirmed. It may be automated, active, or bait.
          <a href="/dispatch/signal-monk/" style="color:var(--teal);">Read Signal Monk &rsaquo;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">1994-01-18</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">reported</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          A supply mark near the Gate E corridor points toward a workshop along the Canal Edge.
          The cache is not physically confirmed. It may be intact, already taken, or deliberately false.
          <a href="/dispatch/canal-cache/" style="color:var(--teal);">Read The Canal Cache &rsaquo;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">1994-02-01 to 1994-02-02</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">confirmed</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Movement from LaSalle peaks overnight and tests the western side of Sector 01.
          Angrignon absorbs part of the movement. Jolicoeur reports contact.
          Saint-Paul-&Eacute;mard holds, but Gate B remains unstable afterward.
          <a href="/dispatch/lasalle-pressure-night/" style="color:var(--teal);">Read The LaSalle Pressure Night &rsaquo;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="term-panel" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag">Unknown / Classified</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">classified / rumored</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.75;">
          Westmount remains redacted in the public terminal. Ville-Marie tunnel stories remain
          unreliable. Olympic Stadium and the Oratory exist as distant rumor layers until dedicated
          archive files decide what is public, what is myth, and what stays sealed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="term-panel">
      <div class="term-header">
        <span class="th__tag th__tag--red">Non-Claims</span>
        <span class="th__rule"></span>
        <span class="th__info">Public Safety</span>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;">
        <ul style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim); line-height:1.8; padding-left:1.2rem;">
          <li>This archive file does not announce a live game server.</li>
          <li>This archive file does not prove a playable custom Montr&eacute;al map.</li>
          <li>This archive file does not claim Project Zomboid export or load-test success.</li>
          <li>This archive file does not explain the exact outbreak origin.</li>
          <li>This archive file records public, reported, rumored, and classified collapse knowledge.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
